  "_comment": [
    "Stair-well camera (schema_version 2) -- the counterexample of review round 2,",
    "defect 2: 'the stair footprint is read as walkable floor on BOTH storeys'.",
    "Derived from tests/fixtures/two_floor_demo.json by dropping the furniture and",
    "putting the only camera over the stair well of the upper landing: the XY",
    "[1.9, 3.0] lies inside the slab opening of floor f1, where the stair's step top",
    "is at 1.959 m while the storey floor is at 2.85 m.  Treating the stair footprint",
    "(blender_agent/checks.py circulation) as free cells of both storeys let this",
    "camera pass every check -- a stand 0.891 m above the tread it would have to",
    "hover over, in a hole of the floor.  The camera rule now asks for a real",
    "support surface under the camera at eye height, so this spec must FAIL",
    "(cameras_stand + the camera being unreachable).",
    "See tests/test_multifloor.py::CameraStandTest.",
    "Everything else (rooms, six doors, the switchback stair and its slab opening)",
    "is the demo scene, so the fix is not allowed to disturb it."
  ],
